              ":question/id": "fe2f3934-fa5c-5a59-be7e-00b6e4889063",
              ":question/math-academy-id": "e-4810",
              ":question/problem": "The matrix $A$ and vectors $\\mathbf{b}_1$, $\\mathbf{b}_2$, $\\mathbf{b}_3$ are given below. Which of the vectors lie in $\\textrm{Null}(A)?$\n\n![](images/53/53e17b54ff077d45401bdc4754ccdcff5d0cad20e8d5b477b7a9e0aec37ab52c.svg)",
              ":question/worked-solution": "A vector $\\mathbf{b}$ lies in $\\textrm{Null}(A)$ if $A\\mathbf{b}=\\mathbf{0}.$ So, we need to compute the product of $A$ and each of the given vectors and check whether it is equal to $\\mathbf{0}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A{b}_{1} & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -6 \\\\ -5 & 10 \\\\ -8 & 16\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-27 \\\\ 45 \\\\ 72\\end{bmatrix}\\ne 0\\,\\times  \\\\ A{b}_{2} & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -6 \\\\ -5 & 10 \\\\ -8 & 16\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}=0\\,\u2713 \\\\ A{b}_{3} & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -6 \\\\ -5 & 10 \\\\ -8 & 16\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-15 \\\\ 25 \\\\ 40\\end{bmatrix}\\ne 0\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $\\mathbf{b}_2$ lies in $\\textrm{Null}(A).$"
            },
            ":knowledge-point/id": "e3c3466c-dfb0-5b5f-b556-ce57a1d78519",
