              ":question/math-academy-id": "e-4807",
              ":question/problem": "The matrix $B$ and the vector $\\mathbf{b}$ are given below. \nDetermine if $\\mathbf{b} \\in \\textrm{Col}(B).$ \nIn the affirmative case, find the values of $x_1$ and $x_2,$ where $x_1$ and $x_2$ are the real numbers such that $\\mathbf{b}=x_1\\mathbf{b}_1+x_2\\mathbf{b}_2,$ and $\\mathbf{b}_1,$ $\\mathbf{b}_2$ are the respective columns of $B.$\n\n![](images/a6/a65747aa11107acc9a05df83473ed0208c23818953b16771b608ec4f572dc7ca.svg)",
              ":question/worked-solution": "In order to determine whether $\\mathbf{b}$ lies in $\\textrm{Col}(B),$ we need to check if the equation $B\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}$ is consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[B \\,|\\, \\mathbf{b}]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[B\\,|\\,b] & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -2 & 7 \\\\ 15 & -6 & 21 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -2 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & \u2194{R}_{3} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -2 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}5{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2} &=7 \\\\ {x}_{2} &=0 \\\\ 0 &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get the true statement $0=0.$ So the system is equivalent to the following:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}5{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2} &=7 \\\\ {x}_{2} &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get $x_2=0.$ Substituting into the first equation gives $x_1=\\dfrac 7 5.$ \n\nSince we have a solution, the equation $B\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}$ is consistent, which implies that $\\mathbf{b}\\in\\textrm{Col}(B).$\n\nMoreover, there is exactly one solution, so we have exactly one way to write $\\mathbf{b}$ as a linear combination of $\\mathbf{b}_1$ and $\\mathbf{b}_2\\mathbin{:}$\n![](images/8a/8a35321d3a29ee86c5af54e23dabd8d3ac93bf7831981507dff3e501796f96a7.svg)"
            },
            ":knowledge-point/id": "5c8e217c-252d-529f-a810-84787e2ee886",
            ":knowledge-point/title": "Determining if a Vector is in the Column Space of a Matrix"
          },
          {
            ":db/id": 17592186119811,
            ":knowledge-point/canonical-example": {
              ":db/id": 17592186119622,
              ":question/id": "12f222d8-5563-544a-8154-fb1f9406b231",
              ":question/math-academy-id": "e-4808",
              ":question/problem": "The matrix $C$ and the vector $\\mathbf{b}$ are given below. Determine if $\\mathbf{b} \\in \\textrm{Col}(C).$ In affirmative case, find the value of $x_1 \\cdot x_2 \\cdot x_3$, where $x_1$, $x_2$, and $x_3$ are real numbers such that $\\mathbf{b}=x_1\\mathbf{c}_1+x_2\\mathbf{c}_3+x_3\\mathbf{c}_3,$ and $\\mathbf{c}_1,$ $\\mathbf{c}_2,$ and $\\mathbf{c}_3$ are the respective columns of $C.$\n\n![](images/02/027332c5a5bdb14913d297e71bc2ac2ae8f846976c1bc3c0c4c569997dcd5b01.svg)",
              ":question/worked-solution": "In order to determine whether $\\mathbf{b}$ lies in $\\textrm{Col}(C),$ we need to check if the equation $C\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}$ is consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[C \\,|\\, \\mathbf{b}]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[C\\,|\\,b] & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 4 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 0 & -4 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 1 & 4\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 1 & 4\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+4{x}_{3} &=5 \\\\ 3{x}_{2}+4{x}_{3} &=1 \\\\ 5{x}_{3} &=5.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get $x_3=1$. Substituting into the second equation gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{2}+4(1) & =1 \\\\ 3{x}_{2} & =-3 \\\\ {x}_{2} & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, from the first equation, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =5-{x}_{2}-4{x}_{3} \\\\  & =5-(-1)-4(1) \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we have a solution, the equation $C\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}$ is consistent, which implies that $\\mathbf{b}\\in\\textrm{Col}(C).$ \n\nMoreover, there is exactly one solution, so we have exactly one way to write $\\mathbf{b}$ as a linear combination of $\\mathbf{c}_1,$ $\\mathbf{c}_2,$ and $\\mathbf{c}_3\\mathbin{:}$\n![](images/4c/4cccd67d5e043d72e0b6949543883e6187d9ef807b7a470146628cbadf7eead7.svg)\n\nFinally, we get $x_1 \\cdot x_2 \\cdot x_3 = 2 \\cdot (-1) \\cdot 1 = -2$."
            },
            ":knowledge-point/id": "87dc8398-fb5c-564b-a796-db15ff30d72c",
            ":knowledge-point/title": "Determining if a Vector Is in the Column Space of a Larger Matrix"
          },
          {
            ":db/id": 17592186119855,
            ":knowledge-point/canonical-example": {
              ":db/id": 17592186119670,
              ":question/id": "b6d52e39-a8a0-5048-80a1-a342a2617e0f",
              ":question/math-academy-id": "e-6208",
              ":question/problem": "Consider the matrix given by ![](images/fd/fdab914fd2a1013caf1d02dc692df697f4c61f61b3aeba6166b471f3833e7811.svg) Determine the value of $k$ for which the vector ![](images/a8/a8acb2b133143150953e861f13e7b9797756c557800b67ca0334a88d26eb3cc9.svg) belongs to $\\textrm{Col}(A).$",
              ":question/worked-solution": "If $\\mathbf{b}$ lies in $\\textrm{Col}(A),$ then the equation $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}$ must be consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[A \\,|\\, \\mathbf{b}]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[A\\,|\\,b] & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 10 \\\\ 3 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 5 & -1 & 2+k\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 10 \\\\ 0 & -8 & -32 \\\\ 5 & -1 & 2+k\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-5{R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 10 \\\\ 0 & -8 & -32 \\\\ 0 & -11 & k-48\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{8}{R}_{2} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -11 & k-48\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+11{R}_{2} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k-4\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} &=10 \\\\ {x}_{2} &=4 \\\\ 0 &=k-4.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nIn order for this system to be consistent, we require $0=k-4,$ which means that $k=4.$"
            },
            ":knowledge-point/id": "a557ee8d-51a9-5387-a28c-67ffefed55b4",
            ":knowledge-point/title": "Determining the Value of an Unknown Given a Vector That\u2019s in the Column Space of a Matrix"
          }
        ],
